# ============================================================================
# P06 - SCHEDULER: drop MTK scheduler tracers  [EXPERIMENTAL / UNVERIFIED]
# ============================================================================
# WHAT IT CHANGES
#   CONFIG_MTK_SCHED_TRACERS=y  ->  # CONFIG_MTK_SCHED_TRACERS is not set
#
#   baseline evidence (kernel source, commit 9b1c9a53):
#     k65v1_64_bsp_defconfig:30   CONFIG_MTK_SCHED_TRACERS=y
#     Neighbouring MTK scheduler options that are NOT touched:
#       k65v1_64_bsp_defconfig:26  CONFIG_MTK_SCHED_EXTENSION=y
#       k65v1_64_bsp_defconfig:27  CONFIG_MTK_IDLE_BALANCE_ENHANCEMENT=y
#       k65v1_64_bsp_defconfig:28  CONFIG_MTK_SCHED_INTEROP=y
#       k65v1_64_bsp_defconfig:29  CONFIG_MTK_SCHED_LB_ENHANCEMENT=y
#       k65v1_64_bsp_defconfig:31  CONFIG_MTK_SCHED_CPU_PREFER=y
#       k65v1_64_bsp_defconfig:32  CONFIG_MTK_SCHED_BIG_TASK_MIGRATE=y
#
# GATE - VERIFY THE SYMBOL'S BLAST RADIUS BEFORE APPLYING
#   The defconfig line proves the symbol exists and is on. It does NOT by
#   itself prove the symbol only wraps tracepoints. Confirm with:
#     grep -rn 'MTK_SCHED_TRACERS' kernel/sched/ drivers/ vendor/ 2>/dev/null
#   If that grep shows MTK_SCHED_TRACERS gating anything other than trace /
#   debug instrumentation - in particular anything that participates in load
#   balancing, task placement or the MTK big-task migration logic - then
#   DROP THIS PATCH. It is not worth the risk on that evidence, and the
#   honest outcome is to drop it rather than to assume.
#
# WHY IT SHOULD HELP ON A 4 GB MT6765V
#   Conditional on that gate passing: MTK's scheduler tracers are debugging
#   hooks added to MTK's scheduling decisions. Instrumentation on the
#   scheduler path means extra branches evaluated per scheduling event on the
#   hottest code path in the kernel, plus tracepoint plumbing and string
#   tables. On a device whose performance budget is dominated by the 6x A55,
#   removing per-schedule-point work from that path is directionally right,
#   and it also shrinks vmlinux.
#   As with P03, expect this to be SMALL. The justification is "shipping
#   debug instrumentation in a production kernel is not free and we do not
#   use it", not "this will show up in a benchmark".
#
# WHAT WOULD VERIFY OR REFUTE IT
#   size vmlinux / ls -l arch/arm64/boot/Image   (code size drop)
#   Baseline vs patched, identical workload:
#     grep -E 'ctxt' /proc/stat       (context switches - should be ~equal)
#     cat /proc/pressure/cpu
#     dumpsys gfxinfo <pkg> framestats
#   Also confirm nothing you need breaks: vendor perfetto/atrace sched
#   tracing loses these MTK-specific points (generic sched points survive).
#   If size barely moves and frame times are within noise, drop the patch.
#
# RISK
#   Loss of vendor-specific sched trace points in perfetto/atrace. If the
#   project's own tracing or profiling pipeline depends on them, this patch
#   costs more than it saves and should be dropped.
# ============================================================================

# CONFIG_MTK_SCHED_TRACERS is not set
